 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Heitz et al. in the context of efficient scene appearance aggregation for level-of-detail rendering. It builds upon the SGGX distribution [Heitz et al. 2015] to provide a flexible representation for surface normals in participating media [S1, unofficial].
+The method uses a mixture of the SGGX distribution introduced by Heitz et al. [Heitz et al. 2015] to represent the marginal distribution of surface normals in participating media [S1, unofficial]. It was presented in the context of efficient scene appearance aggregation for level-of-detail rendering [S1, unofficial].
 
